A||||2||Gold-86SE||Fiero down, your opinion needed.||||9||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||05-02-2000||10:30 AM||||My 86 has decided to crap out on me.<P>First a little history, I bought it from a fella in January, but since I bought it I have had to do one thing after another.<P>The car was pretty much taken care of exterior and interior wise, but as for the maintenance aspect of the Fiero that is another story. The prior owner(s) did not mechanically appreciate the Fiero and my continual maintenance proves that.<P>The latest breakdown.<BR>The muffler has died on me, and the back pressure keeps blowing the straight pipe apart (the straight pipe replaces the cat - so my 86 is running w/o the cat) at the adjoining 'C' clamp. I also discovered that both exhaust headers are cracked and leaking. And this has all happened when I have NO MONEY. Which, needless to say, leaves me sitting for about 30-45 days and I ain't happy about it.<P>However, since I am down for awhile it does give me the opportunity to explore possibilities. My preference is to spend worthwhile money to repair/replace the parts to gain performance, yet I don't really know much about exhaust performance.<P>Here is some preliminary(sp) data that my lovely and gracious wife retrieved for me.<P>Midas is 216.60, which includes tax, labor, cat, and muffler. For 12 bucks more I can get their performance muffler, called (I think) Rhino.  What do you guys know about Midas, and what about their performance muffler?<P>At another shop (much cheaper, but get what you pay for) for about 120, includes labor, cat (the cat is from advance auto parts), and muffler. What do you know about advance cats?<P>Part of me, wants to spend very little money so that I can save up for a better exhaust system, but the other part of me says fix it a little better, then when the opportunity arrives work on it then.<P>I am kinda in an exhaust quagmire, what do you guys think I should do?||||reg||9
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-02-2000||01:26 PM||||The only experience I've had with Midas is the pipes fall apart after a year and they will gladly give you a free muffler so you can spend $200 for new pipes (which are not guarenteed)the next year.<P>New stock exhaust manafolds are ~$200 each plus installation.  Headders are ~$500-$700 depending on whose you buy. Catalytic convertor, I paid $98 at NAPA.  Borla Exhaust (cat back) was ~$500. With a million mile guarentee  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>So for $1000 you can get a brand new exhaust.<P>As you say you get what you pay for.<P>What is causing all the back pressure??? Plugged muffler?<P>With no $$, I'd go for the dollar savings cause it going to cost too much to do it better.  Look around for other exhaust manafolds and replace them when you get the chance and time.<P>Who knows the $120 system may last a couple of years.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||05-02-2000||06:35 PM||||The stock exhaust manifolds can be welded for about $30 and you can remove the restrictions in side for free and gain about 5-8 hp||||reg||1
